menu "RoverCore VCU"

config ROVERCORE_ACTUATORS_PERMITTED
    bool "Let SERVO_PWR_EN / ACT_OE_N follow the enable (NOT in this firmware stage)"
    default n
    help
        Off: the outputs stay locked (SERVO_PWR_EN low, ACT_OE_N high) in every state, also after a valid
        enable sequence. Must stay off until the PWM stage defines the neutral first pulse and the limits,
        and until the carrier measurements of the shutdown are done (docs/vcu/firmware-plan.md).

config ROVERCORE_BENCH_DEVKIT_ONLY
    bool "Bench build for a bare DevKit without carrier"
    default n
    depends on !ROVERCORE_ACTUATORS_PERMITTED
    help
        Internal pull-up on GPIO10 (button released) and pull-down on GPIO18 (ACT_ARMED low), and VBAT reported
        as 12.0 V, so the enable sequence can be exercised with a push button on GPIO10 and a wire on GPIO18.
        Never for the carrier: the carrier has its own pull resistors and real VBAT measurement.

config ROVERCORE_DIAG_PERIOD_MS
    int "Diagnostic line period (ms)"
    default 500
    range 100 10000

endmenu
